{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1507864859,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNjUxNTgyNjc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1898","origin":"github"},"title":"DLMSEP#3: report that there is more results which aren't shown","message":"#### What is the problem?\nATM, naive (or even experienced) user might assume that whatever he sees is all matching records.  But by default it is not so -- only up to 10(?) reported, and there is no notification that there might be more!  The easiest way would be, if # of results == max-nresults, add a message \"There might be more results, please set --max-nresults to higher value or 0 to see all\" or something like that.  It would immediately\n- trigger attention to presence of such a flag\n- break any script which just pipes output somewhere for processing, so they will make sure to specify --max-nresult","files":null}]}